 ## Overview
-Tile-Local Bin Construction assigns Gaussian-tile intersection entries to coarse depth bins within each tile and constructs a flattened tile-bin-major pair stream using direct atomic operations for count and scatter [S1]. It solves the problem of organizing splats for cache-efficient compositing by grouping them into depth-ordered buckets, serving as the foundational data structure for subsequent rasterization passes [S1]. It is distinguished from its siblings by its reliance on direct atomics for the count/scatter phase, which provides the default performance baseline on modern hardware [S1].
